  cost</span></p>
  </td>
 </tr>
</table>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  The director of the department of
community and human services is authorized to charge and collect a reduced
amount for low-income persons whose income, adjusted for family size, is at or
less than eighty percent of the state of Washington median income.  Persons who
are determined to be indigent, by reason of receiving public assistance shall
not be charged a fee.  (Ord. 17292 § 32, 2012:  Ord. 13663 § 2, 1999.  Formerly
K.C.C. 4.96.010).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<h1><a name="_Toc319933163"></a><a name="_Toc54697858"><span style='font-size:
12.0pt'>4A.630           DEPARTMENT OF JUDICIAL ADMINISTRATION FEES</span></a></h1>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.630.010    Forms,
providing.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.630.020    Failure
to bring case to completion.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.630.030    Transmittal
of legal case records for appeal.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.630.040    Issuance
of civil warrants, subpoenas and citations, documents                                              needing
a clerk's seal.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.630.050    Participants
in continuing legal education program.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.630.060    Documents
filed with the clerk's office that require extra handling.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.630.070    Mandatory
arbitration request.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.630.080    Trial
de novo of arbitration award.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.630.090    Service
of bulk user access.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.630.095    Civil
and criminal case index data access subscription.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.630.100    Domestic
violence prevention account revenues administration.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.630.110    Noncertified
copies of legal case files provision.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.630.120    Trust
payments through the superior court registry processing.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.630.130    Domestic
relations cases for courthouse facilitator program.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.630.140    Voucher
system for payment of services provision.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.630.160    Conversion
of file exhibits.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.630.170    Expedited
clerk services.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.630.180    Customer
requests via the mail.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.630.190    Preparing
and providing copies of documents to the court.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.630.200    Preparing
and providing report of new cases or new judgments filed                                      in
superior court – evaluation, research or programming –                                                        administration
fee for data dissemination requests of publicly                                                  accessible
superior court records data.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.630.300    Collection.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.630.310    Waiver.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.630.010  Forms,
providing.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The department of judicial administration is hereby
authorized to assess a fee for providing forms used in King County superior court. 
The charge shall be fifty cents per page to cover all costs associated with
forms' reaction and distribution.  (Ord. 17150 § 4, 2011:  Ord. 9349 § 1, 1990. 
Formerly K.C.C. 4.71.010).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>4A.630.020 
Failure to bring case to completion.</b>  </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>The <span style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>department
of judicial administration is hereby authorized to assess a fee to either
parties to an action filed with the superior court  or attorneys representing
the parties, or both, who fail to bring cases to completion because of failure
to appear for trial, failure to file final order on settlement, failure to
follow case schedule, failure to file final judgment or appeal following a
arbitration award; lack of action of record or failure to comply with
court-ordered deadlines for reports.  The fee assessed shall be fifty dollars
to cover costs associated with identifying these cases and notifying either the
parties or the attorneys, or both.  (Ord. 16966 § 3, 2010:  Ord. 14905 § 6,
2004:  Ord. 13662 § 4, 1999:  Ord. 13330 § 16, 1998.  Formerly K.C.C. 4.71.050).</span></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>4A.630.030 
Transmittal of legal case records for appeal.</b>  The department of judicial
administration is hereby authorized to assess a fee to parties requesting
transmittal of legal case records to the Washington state court of appeals or
Washington state supreme court as part of an appeal from the decision in a King
County superior court case.  The fee assessed for transmittal of the records
shall be the actual cost to the department for the transmittal of the records. 
(Ord. 18818 § 2, 2018:  Ord. 14905 § 8, 2004:  Ord. 13330 § 18, 1998.  Formerly
K.C.C. 4.71.060).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.630.040  Issuance
of civil warrants, subpoenas and citations, documents needing a clerk's seal.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
The department of judicial administration is hereby authorized to assess a fee
for issuance of civil warrants, subpoenas and citations, and for each document
needing a clerk's seal.  In accordance with RCW 36.18.050, the fee assessed for
issuance of civil warrants, subpoenas and citations shall be the same as the
fee established for the issuance of a writ of attachment as specified in RCW
36.18.016.  (Ord. 17150 § 8, 2011: Ord. 13330 § 20, 1998.  Formerly K.C.C.
4.71.070).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>4A.630.050 
Participants in continuing legal education program.</b>  The department of
judicial administration is hereby authorized to assess a fee to participants in
the department's continuing legal education program.  The fee assessed for
participation in the program shall be two hundred fifty dollars to cover all
costs of materials and presentation.  (Ord. 19701 § 1, 2023:  Ord. 16967 § 3,
2010:  Ord. 13330 § 24, 1998.  Formerly K.C.C. 4.71.090).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.630.060  Documents
filed with clerk's office that require extra handling.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The
department of judicial administration is hereby authorized to assess a fee to
anyone who files a document that requires special handling because of errors,
failure to follow court rules or statutes or lack of completeness.  The
department shall make the decision to return the document to the filer on a
case-by-case basis.  The fee assessed for a document that requires extra
handling because of errors, failure to follow court rules or statutes or lack
of completeness shall be fifteen dollars for each incorrect or incomplete
document to cover all costs of the extra handling required.  (Ord. 17150 § 11,
2011:  Ord. 16291 § 3, 2008:  Ord. 14905 § 10, 2004:  Ord. 13991 § 2, 2000: 
Ord. 13330 § 26, 1998:  Ord. 8752 §§ 1-3, 1988:  Formerly K.C.C. 2.12.150. 
Formerly K.C.C. 4.71.100).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>4A.630.070 
Mandatory arbitration request.</b>  The department of judicial administration
is hereby authorized to assess and collect a fee for filing a request for
mandatory arbitration, as authorized in RCW 36.18.016.  The fee will be two
hundred fifty dollars.  (Ord. 18816 § 2, 2018:  Ord. 14447 § 2, 2002:  Ord.
13842 § 2, 2000.  Formerly K.C.C. 4.71.115).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>4A.630.080 
Trial de novo of arbitration award.</b>  The department of judicial
administration is hereby authorized to assess and collect a fee for filing a
request for a trial de novo of an arbitration award, as authorized under RCW
36.18.016.  The fee shall be four hundred dollars.  (Ord. 18816 § 4, 2018:  Ord.
13563 § 2, 1999.  Formerly K.C.C. 4.71.120).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.630.090  Service
of bulk user access.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The department of judicial administration is hereby
authorized to assess a fee for the service of bulk user access to superior
court records managed by the department of judicial administration.  The fee
assessed shall be two hundred fifty dollars per year, to cover the costs
associated with providing this service.  A fee of twenty-five dollars per month
shall be charged to users who do not require bulk access for an entire year. 
(Ord. 13990 § 2, 2000.  Formerly K.C.C. 4.71.150).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.630.095 
Civil and criminal case index data access subscription</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=X-NONE
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A. 
The department of judicial administration is hereby authorized to assess a
subscription fee for providing access to civil and criminal case index data.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=X-NONE
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B. 
The criminal case data index consists of an index of names of defendants and
their associated criminal cases and charges in superior court, updated on a
regular basis.  The annual subscription fee for the criminal case data index
shall be three thousand six hundred dollars.  The semiannual subscription fee
for the criminal case data index shall be one thousand eight hundred dollars. 
The fee for a single criminal case index report shall be one thousand five
hundred dollars.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=X-NONE
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C. 
The general case data index consists of an index of names of litigants and
their associated cases in superior court, updated on a regular basis.  The
annual subscription fee for the general case data index shall be one thousand
eight hundred dollars.  The semiannual subscription fee for the general case
data index shall be nine hundred dollars.  The fee for a single general case
index report shall be seven hundred fifty dollars.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=X-NONE
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            D. 
The probate case data index consists of an index of the prior week's probate
filings in superior court, updated on a regular basis.  The annual subscription
fee for the probate case data index shall be one thousand two hundred dollars. 
The semiannual subscription fee for the probate case data index shall be six
hundred dollars.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=X-NONE
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            </span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>E.</span><span
lang=X-NONE style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>  The department of judicial administration shall establish a procedure
for the creation of the indexes and index updates, administration of
subscriptions, and collection of subscription fees.</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
(Ord. 19373 § 2, 2021:  Ord. 19194 § 2, 2020).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>4A.630.100 
Domestic violence prevention account revenues administration.</b>  The
department of judicial administration is hereby authorized to retain five
percent of the county's portion of the domestic violence prevention account fee
authorized under RCW 36.18.016.  (Ord. 17150 § 15, 2011: Ord. 15272 § 2, 2005. 
Formerly K.C.C. 4.71.200).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.630.110  Noncertified
copies of legal case files provision.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The department of
judicial administration is hereby authorized to assess a fee for providing
noncertified copies of legal case files.  Copies prepared by department staff from
hard copy, also known as paper, files or copied remotely using the department's
online electronic court record system from a site outside the department's
facilities shall be subject to a fee in accordance with RCW 36.18.016(4). 
Self-service copies of files using the self-service copying machines provided
by the department shall be fifteen cents per page. The department of judicial
administration shall establish a procedure for the collection of the fees in
this section.  (Ord. 17921 § 2, 2014:  Ord. 17150 § 17, 2011:  Ord. 16289 § 2,
2008:  Ord. 14905 § 12, 2004:  Ord. 10644 § 1, 1992:  Ord. 9774 § 1, 1991. 
Formerly K.C.C. 4.73.010).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.630.120  Trust
payments through the superior court registry processing.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            </span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>A. 
The department of judicial administration is hereby authorized to assess
service fees for reimbursement for the actual costs incurred by the county to
process trust payments through the superior court registry.  </span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  The
following fees may be assessed:</span></p>

<p class=MsoBodyText3><span style='font-size:12.0pt'>              1.  Two
dollars per payment if a child support payment greater than twenty-five dollars
and less than or equal to one hundred and fifty dollars is made and;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  Ten
dollars per payment for all child support payments exceeding one hundred and
fifty dollars and for all other types of payments which exceed twenty-five
dollars;</span></p>

<p class=MsoBodyText3><span style='font-size:12.0pt'>            C.  This
section applies to all payments received for processing through the superior
court registry, except for any payment whose processing costs are otherwise
reimbursed to the county from other sources.  (Ord. 17150 § 19, 2011:  Ord.
13330 § 10, 1998:  Ord. 6242 § 1, 1982.  Formerly K.C.C. 4.76.010).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.630.130  Domestic
relations cases for courthouse facilitator program.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
The department of judicial administration is authorized to assess a surcharge
of twenty dollars to superior court filing fees for domestic relations cases
filed under Title 26 RCW, to be used for funding the courthouse facilitator
program which provides basic services to pro se litigants in family law cases. 
(Ord. 17150 § 21, 2011:  Ord. 15272 § 3, 2005:  Ord. 13330 § 8, 1998:  Ord.
11136 § 1, 1993.  Formerly K.C.C. 4.79.010).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>4A.630.140 
Voucher system for payment of services provision.</b>  The department of
judicial administration is hereby authorized to assess a fee for the service of
providing a voucher system for payment of services provided by the department. 
The fee assessed shall be ten percent of the yearly charges to the voucher
account, to cover some of the expenses involved in processing the vouchers and
sending invoices.  (Ord. 17150 § 23, 2011:  Ord. 13662 § 9, 1999.  Formerly
K.C.C. 4.83.010).</span></p>

<p class=MsoBodyText3><span style='font-size:12.0pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoBodyText3><span style='font-size:12.0pt'>            <b>4A.630.160 
Conversion of file exhibits.</b>  The department of judicial administration is
hereby authorized to assess a fee for the conversion of items that are
inappropriate for filing in the court file to file exhibits.  This fee is
assessed in accordance with RCW 36.18.016(11).  The fee assessed shall be thirty
dollars.  (Ord. 18815 § 2, 2018:  Ord. 17150 § 27, 2011:  Ord. 14905 § 17,
2004.  Formerly K.C.C. 4.83.040).</span></p>

<p class=MsoBodyText3><span style='font-size:12.0pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>4A.630.170 
Expedited clerk services.</b>  The department of judicial administration is
hereby authorized to assess a fee for providing clerk services on an expedited
basis.  The fee assessed shall be forty dollars.  (Ord. 19702 § 1, 2023:  Ord.
17150 § 29, 2011:  Ord. 16290 § 3, 2008.  Formerly K.C.C. 4.83.060).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>4A.630.180 
Customer requests via the mail.</b>  The department of judicial administration
is hereby authorized to assess a fee for fulfilling customer requests via the
mail.  The fee assessed shall be seven dollars per transaction and unless
postage is provided by the customer, postage will be charged at a rate of three
dollars per transaction.  (Ord. 17150 § 31, 2011:  Ord. 16293 § 3, 2008. 
Formerly K.C.C. 4.83.070).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>4A.630.190 
Preparing and providing documents to the court.</b>  The department of judicial
administration is hereby authorized to assess and collect a fee for preparing
and providing copies of documents to the court.  The fee only applies when
documents have been electronically submitted to the clerk by parties who wish
to have copies provided to the respective judicial officer.  The fee assessed
shall be forty dollars per submission.   (Ord. 19703 § 1, 2023:  Ord. </span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>19193 <span
style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span> 1, 2020:  <span style='letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>Ord. 17150 § 33, 2011:  Ord. 16297 § 3, 2008.  Formerly K.C.C. 4.83.080).</span></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.630.200  Preparing
and providing report of new cases or new judgments filed in superior court –
evaluation, research or programming – administration fee for data dissemination
requests of publicly available superior court records data.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The
department of judicial administration is hereby authorized to assess and
collect a fee for preparing and providing a report of new cases filed in
superior court or new judgments filed in superior court.  The fee shall be five
dollars per report.  The department of judicial administration may assess and
collect a fee for evaluation, research or programming of fifty-five dollars per
hour, and an administration fee of fifty dollars per report, for data
dissemination requests of publicly accessible superior court records data.  (Ord.
18817 § 2, 2018:  Ord. 17150 § 35, 2011:  Ord. 16968 § 3, 2011.  Formerly
K.C.C. 4.83.090).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.630.300  Collection.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
The department of judicial administration shall establish a procedure for the
collection of the fees in this chapter.  (Ord. 17150 § 37, 2011:  Ord. 9349 §
3, 1990.  Formerly K.C.C. 4.71.030).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>4A.630.310 
Waiver.  </b>The department of judicial administration is authorized to waive
all or part of the fees authorized in the [this] chapter.  (Ord. 17150 § 38,
2011).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

