<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.632.210    Waver.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.632.010 
Purpose.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The purpose of this chapter is to authorize the
superior court to assess fees for reimbursement of costs incurred by the county
for:  adoption services including flat search fee, consultation and
confirmation of consents; dissolution services including:  orientation,
mediation, one party and two party evaluations, witness fees for testimony
provided by family court services staff, and marriage waivers.  Such service
fees shall be the responsibility of the party or parties requesting the
service.  (Ord. 17150 § 41, 2011:  Ord. 10643 § 1, 1992:  Ord. 6241 § 1, 1982.
Formerly K.C.C. 4.72.010).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>4A.632.020 
Forms, providing.</b>  The superior court is authorized to charge a fee for
providing forms.  The charge shall be fifty cents per page.  (Ord. 17150 § 42,
2011).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.632.030  Family
court services.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Fees for family court services dissolution matters are
established as follows:        The superior court shall prepare a fee schedule
charging no more than two hundred dollars, per hour, for:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A. 
Dissolution services including:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  Mediation
and evaluation orientation;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  Mediation
services;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  Evaluation
services;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              4.  Dissolution
one and two party evaluations;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              5.  Witness
fees for court testimony provided by family court services staff; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              6.  Marriage
waivers.  (Ord. 17150 § 44, 2011:  Ord. 16982 § 2, 1010:  Ord. 16304 § 1,
2008:  Ord. 14798 § 2, 2003:  Ord. 13330 § 2, 1998:  Ord. 10643 § 2, 1992: 
Ord. 6241 § 2, 1982.  Formerly K.C.C.4.72.020 ).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>4A.632.040 
Family court services adoption matters.</b>  Fees for family court services
adoption matters are established as follows:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            The superior
court shall prepare a fee schedule charging no more than one hundred fifty
dollars, per hour, for adoption services, including:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  Confirmation
of birth parent consent reports in all independent nonagency adoptions;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  Stepparent
adoption reports; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  Other
services as ordered by the court.  (Ord. 17150 § 46, 2011:  Ord. 16982 § 4,
2011.  Formerly K.C.C. 4.72.021).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>4A.632.050 
Adoption checklist and file review.</b>  The superior court is hereby
authorized [to] assess a fee of fifteen dollars for the completion of an
adoption checklist and file review, to be completed prior to final hearing. 
(Ord. 14791 § 1, 2003.  Formerly K.C.C. 4.72.022).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.632.060  Adoption
case record search.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The superior court shall assess a flat search fee for
each adoption case record search at the rate established by RCW 36.18.020.  (Ord.
17150 § 49, 2011:  Ord. 13330 § 4, 1998:  Ord. 10643 § 3, 1992.  Formerly
K.C.C. 4.72.025).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>4A.632.070 
Fee for nonidentifying adoption searches by the superior court.</b>  The
superior court is hereby authorized to charge a flat fee of sixty dollars for
each nonidentifying adoption search performed.  (Ord. 16969 § 2, 2010:  Ord.
14791 § 2, 2003.  Formerly K.C.C. 4.72.026).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>4A.632.080 
Fee - visit with superior court paralegal for adoption related services.</b> 
The superior court is hereby authorized to charge a user fee of up to twenty
dollars per visit with the superior court adoption paralegal, for adoption
related services as authorized under RCW 26.12.220.  Retained revenues shall be
used to support costs associated with operating family court operations.  (Ord.
16970 § 2, 2010.  Formerly K.C.C. 4.72.027).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>4A.632.090 
Fee for registering confidential intermediaries with the superior court.</b> 
The superior court is hereby authorized to charge an annual fee of one hundred
dollars to each confidential intermediary who works with family court
services.  (Ord. 14791 § 3, 2003.  Formerly K.C.C. 4.72.028).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>4A.632.100 
Fee - facilitator services to review domestic cases documentation.</b>  A fee
of thirty dollars is imposed for services rendered to review documentation
related to domestic cases before finalization, in accordance with RCW
26.12.240.</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'><a
name=attachment></a>  (Ord. 17150 § 52, 2011:  Ord. 16980 § 2, 2010:  Ord.
16305 § 1, 2008.  Formerly K.C.C. 4.72.032).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>4A.632.110 
Fee - facilitator services to review domestic cases documentation - per visit.</b> 
            A.  The superior court is hereby authorized to charge a user fee of
up to thirty dollars per visit for facilitator services, as authorized under
RCW 26.12.240.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  </span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>A fee
of thirty dollars is imposed for facilitator services rendered to review
documentation related to domestic cases before finalization, in accordance with
RCW 26.12.240.</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  (Ord.
17150 § 54, 2011:  Ord. 16979 § 2, 2010:  Ord. 16306 § 2, 2008.  Formerly
K.C.C. 4.72.034).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>4A.632.120 
Parenting seminars.</b>  The superior court is hereby authorized to charge a
parenting seminar registration fee of eighty dollars per participant for those
who attend the parenting seminar provided by King County superior court.  Retained
revenues shall be used to support operating costs associated with family court
operations.  (Ord. 19849 § 2, 2024:  Ord. 16972 § 2, 2010.  Formerly K.C.C.
4.72.042).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>4A.632.130 
Family law orientation.</b>  The superior court is hereby authorized to charge
a fee of up to twenty dollars per person to attend a family law orientation
provided by King County superior court family court operations.  This fee is
authorized by RCW 26.12.260, 26.12.220 and 26.12.240.  (Ord. 17150 § 57, 2011: 
Ord. 16983 § 2, 2010.  Formerly K.C.C. 4.72.045).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>4A.632.200 
Collection.</b>  The superior court is responsible for collection of fees
authorized in this chapter.  (Ord. 17150 § 59, 2011).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>4A.632.210 
Waiver.</b>  The superior court is authorized to waive all or part of the fees
authorized in this chapter based on the parties' ability to pay.  (Ord. 17150 §
58, 2011)</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<h1><a name="_Toc319933165"></a><a name="_Toc54697860"><span style='font-size:
12.0pt'>4A.634           DISTRICT COURT FEES</span></a></h1>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.634.010    Surcharge
established -- collection.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.634.020    Surcharge
- small claims court.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.634.030    Domestic
violence prevention cases.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.634.100    Filing
electronic that requires special handling - Attorney who files                                          paper
document if electronic filing required and approval waiver not                                       obtained.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.634.010 
Surcharge established -- collection.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The King County council
hereby establishes a surcharge of ten dollars to district court civil filing
fees to be used for funding dispute resolution services.  This surcharge shall
be collected by the King County district court which shall establish a procedure
for collection and segregation of this surcharge in accordance with chapter
7.75 RCW.  (Ord. 13662 § 2, 1999:  Ord. 12214 § 1, 1996:  Ord. 11158 § 1,
1993:  Ord. 10670 § 1, 1992: Ord. 9916 § 1, 1991.  Formerly K.C.C. 4.82.010).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>4A.634.020 
Surcharge - small claims court.  </b>The King County council hereby establishes
a surcharge of fifteen dollars to small claims court filing fees to be used for
funding dispute resolution services.  This surcharge shall be collected by the
King County district court, which shall establish a procedure for collection
and segregation of this surcharge in accordance with chapter 7.75 RCW.  (Ord. 18545
§ 1, 2017:  Ord. 12214 § 2, 1996.  Formerly K.C.C. 4.82.020).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>4A.634.030 
Domestic violence prevention cases.</b></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  The
following district court administrative fee for district court costs is
established to cover administrative district court costs in domestic violence
cases:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                        District
court administrative court cost fee                                    $63.00</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  This fee
may be imposed by the district court against the respondent in domestic
violence cases as authorized by state law.  (Ord. 16288 § 3, 2008. Formerly
K.C.C. 4.79.020).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.634.100  Filing electronic that requires
special handling - Attorney who files paper document if electronic filing
required and approval waiver not obtained.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  The
district court may assess a fee of twenty dollars to anyone who files an
electronic document that requires special handling because of errors, failure
to follow court rules or statutes or lack of completeness</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  The
district court may assess a fee of fifty dollars to each attorney who files a
paper document that is required by court rule to be electronically filed,
without obtaining an approved waiver from electronic filing from the district
court.  (Ord. 17922 § 2, 2014).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<h1><a name="_Toc54697862"><span style='font-size:12.0pt'>4A.650           PUBLIC
HEALTH</span></a></h1>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.650.010    Notary
services fee.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.650.100    Medical
examiner report fee.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.650.110    Medical
examiner reports fee - waiver.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.650.150    Reporting
a death to the medical examiner's office for remains to be                                      buried,            cremated,
or otherwise disposed.</span></p>

<p class=MsoBodyText3><span style='font-size:12.0pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>4A.650.010  Notary services fee.</b>  A
person who receives notary services from the director of the Seattle-King
County department of public health in accordance with chapters 26.26 RCW and
70.08 RCW shall be charged a fee of eight dollars.  (Ord. 16971 § 3, 2010. 
Formerly K.C.C. 4.120.010).</span></p>

<p class=MsoBodyText3><span style='font-size:12.0pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.650.100 
Medical examiner report fees.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  Any
person, agent or company who requests and receives a copy of an autopsy report
in accordance with RCW 68.50.105 shall be charged a fee of fifty dollars.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  Any
person, agent or company who requests and receives a copy of a determination
shall be charged a fee of twenty dollars.  (Ord. 18388 § 1, 2016:  Ord. 17292 §
16, 2012:  Ord. 16965 § 2, 2010:  Ord. 15953 § 2, 2007:  Ord. 11137 § 1 (part),
1993.  Formerly K.C.C. 4.88.010).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.650.110 
Medical examiner reports fee - waiver.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The director of the
Seattle-King County department of public health is authorized to waive the fees
established by K.C.C. 4A.650.100, when the reports are requested and received
by the decedent's attending physician or by law enforcement agencies or
officials conducting criminal investigations or prosecutions.  (Ord. 17292 §
18, 2012:  Ord. 15953 § 3, 2007:  Ord. 11137 § 1 (part), 1993.  Formerly K.C.C.
4.88.020).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            <b>4A.650.150 
Reporting a death to the medical examiner's office for remains to be buried,
cremated, or otherwise disposed.</b>  A person reporting a death to the medical
examiner's office of a person whose remains are to be buried, cremated, or
otherwise disposed of under K.C.C. 2.35A.100, shall be charged a fee of one
hundred dollars.  (Ord. 19709 § 1, 2023:  Ord. 18388 <span style='letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>§</span> 2, 2016:  Ord. 18103 <span style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span>
2, 2015:  Ord. 17733 § 16, 2014).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

