<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  Special
circumstances and requests for output products other than those specified in
subsection A. of this section shall be charged a fixed rate, determined by the
department of information technology, based on the prevailing labor and
resource costs.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  Based on
their unique requirements, cash-on-delivery and non-King County customers may
be assessed a fee of up to ten percent to cover undistributed overhead.  (Ord.
18394 § 2, 2016:  Ord. 17292 § 13, 2012:  Ord. 12918 § 1, 1997:  Ord. 11131 §
1, 1993:  Ord. 10651 § 1, 1992:  Ord. 10173 § 1, 1991:  Ord. 9874 § 1, 1991: 
Ord. 9222 § 1, 1989:  Ord. 8751 § 1, 1988:  Ord. 8326 § 1, 1987:  Ord. 7946,
1987:  Ord. 7421 § 1, 1985:  Ord. 7011 § 1, 1984:  Ord. 6666 § 2, 1984. 
Formerly K.C.C. 4.80.020).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:103.5pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-103.5pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<h1><a name="_Toc54697864"><span style='font-size:12.0pt'>4A.670           NATURAL
RESOURCES AND PARKS</span></a></h1>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoBodyText3 style='margin-left:1.5in;text-indent:-1.5in'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt'>            4A.670.100    Sewer rate.</span></p>

<p class=MsoBodyText3 style='margin-left:1.5in;text-indent:-1.5in'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt'>            4A.670.110    Financial plan - water
quality program.</span></p>

<p class=MsoBodyText3 style='margin-left:1.5in;text-indent:-1.5in'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt'>            4A.670.120    Equity among county and
noncounty customers - wastewater management program.</span></p>

<p class=MsoBodyText3 style='margin-left:1.5in;text-indent:-1.5in'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt'>            4A.670.200    Noxious weed control program
assessment.</span></p>

<p class=MsoBodyText3 style='margin-left:1.5in;text-indent:-1.5in'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt'>            4A.670.300    C&amp;D wastes disposal (construction
and demolition wastes disposal) - fee - use.</span></p>

<p class=MsoBodyText3><span style='font-size:12.0pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.670.100 
Sewer rate.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  Having
determined the monetary requirements for the disposal of sewage, the council
hereby adopts a 2027 sewer rate of seventy dollars and sixty-five cents per
residential customer equivalent per month.  Once a sewer rate ordinance becomes
effective, the clerk of the council is directed to deliver a copy of that
ordinance to each agency having an agreement for sewage disposal with King
County.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            </span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>B.  The King County
council approves the application of Statement No. 62 of the Governmental
Accounting Standards Board (GASB-62) as it pertains to regulatory assets and
liabilities to treat pollution remediation obligations and RainWise Program
expenditures and strategic planning costs as regulatory assets, recovered
ratably over the life of the underlying financing, and to establish a rate
stabilization reserve for the purpose of leveling rates between years.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>            C.  As required for GASB-62
application, amounts are to be placed in the rate stabilization reserve from
operating revenues and removed from the calculation of debt service coverage. 
The reserve balance shall be an amount at least sufficient to maintain a level
sewer rate between 2027 and 2028, and shall be used solely for the purposes
of:  maintaining the level sewer rate in 2028; and if additional reserve
balance is available, moderating future rate increases beyond 2028.  The
estimated amount of the reserve, as shown in the financial plan, Attachment A
to<b> </b>Ordinance 20087*, shall be revised in accordance with the 2026-2027
Biennial Budget Ordinance and financial plan.  If the reserve needs to be
reduced to meet debt service coverage requirements for 2026, the county
executive shall notify the council of the change by providing an updated
financial plan.  (Ord. 20087 § 1, 2026:  Ord. 19942 § 1, 2025:  Ord. 19782 § 1,
2024:  Ord. 19623 § 1, 2023:  Ord. 19447 § 1, 2022:  Ord. 19294 § 1, 2021:  Ord.
19106 § 1, 2020:  Ord. 18915 § 1, 2019:  Ord. 18745 § 1, 2018:  Ord. 18537 § 1,
2017:  Ord. 18305 <span style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span> 1, 2016:  Ord.
18064 <span style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span> 1, 2015:  Ord. 17825 § 1,
2014:  Ord. 17606 § 1, 2013:  Ord. 17343 § 1, 2012,  Ord. 17102 § 1, 2011: 
Ord. 16858 § 1, 2010:  Ord. 16554 § 1, 2002:  Ord. 16135 § 1, 2008:  Ord. 15805
§ 1, 2007:  Ord. 15522 § 1, 2006:  Ord. 15384 § 4, 2006:  Ord. 15194 § 1,
2005:  Ord. 14942 § 2, 2004:  Ord. 14676 §  1, 2003:  Ord. 14395 § 1, 2002: 
Ord. 14123 § 1, 2001:  Ord. 13570 § 3, 1999:  Ord. 13227 § 2, 1998:  Ord. 12817
§ 2, 1997:  Ord. 12353 § 2, 1996.  <span style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Formerly
K.C.C. </span>4.90.010).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>*Available
in the King County Archives.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.670.110 
Financial plan - water quality program.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The council hereby
adopts a financial plan for the 1996 water quality program that includes a rate
not to exceed twenty dollars and thirty cent to satisfy the financial
obligations of the wastewater management program.  The executive shall prepare
the 1996 water quality budget and determine specific monetary requirements of
the 1996 sewer program in accordance with this directive.  (Ord. 17292 § 22,
2012:  Ord. 11377 § 2, 1994.  Formerly K.C.C. 4.90.020).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.670.120 
Equity among county and noncounty customers - wastewater management program.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
Council affirms historic Metro policies to equally share responsibilities,
opportunities, costs and risks associated with the wastewater management
program among all component agencies.  The executive shall annually prepare an
assessment of system equity in accordance with the following requirements to
ensure that King <span style='text-transform:uppercase'>c</span>ounty customers
do not bear a disproportionate share of system costs and risks as compared to
customers served outside King County.  The report shall identify:</span></p>

<p class=MsoBodyText3><span style='font-size:12.0pt'>            A.  The annual
and accrued sewer rate benefit associated with use of King County general
obligation bonds on the sewer rate as compared to an estimated rate based
exclusively on revenue bond issuance beginning January 1, 1994; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  An
estimate of the annual and accrued cash value of the rate benefit to non-King
County customers listed by component agency as compared to an estimated rate
based exclusively on revenue bond issuance; and </span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  Status of
efforts made to resolve any inequities identified between King County and
non-King County component agencies during the year.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            D.  Status of
efforts made by adjoining jurisdictions or non-King County component agencies
to help King County locate biosolid handling and disposal facilities within
their jurisdictional boundaries; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            E.  The
executive shall not amend or modify any agreement with a component agency
serving non-King County residents unless the agreement also includes provisions
to resolve any inequities favoring non-King County customers as described in
the annual report.  (Ord. 17292 § 24, 2012:  Ord. 11377 § 3, 1994.  Formerly
K.C.C. 4.90.030).</span></p>

<p class=MsoBodyText3><span style='font-size:12.0pt;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>4A.670.200 
Noxious weed control program assessment.</b></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  An
assessment for the King County noxious weed control program of eight dollars
and one hundred twenty-two one thousandths cents per parcel and fifty-eight cents
per acre on all property not classified as forest land shall be imposed
annually.  Property classified as forest land, as defined in RCW 84.33.035,
that is used solely for the planting, growing or harvesting of trees and that
is typified by canopies so dense as to prohibit the growth of an understory
shall be assessed at the rate of eighty-one and two one-thousandths cents per
parcel and five and eight one-thousandths cents per acre.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  The amount
of the assessment shall constitute a lien against any property for which the
assessment has not been paid by the date it is due, as provided in RCW
17.10.240.  A notice of lien shall be sent to each owner of such a property.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  Lands
owned by the federal government or lands owned by federally recognized tribes
or members of such tribes as are located within the historical boundaries of a
reservation shall not be assessed for the noxious weed control program.  (Ord. 20004
§ 2, 2025:  Ord. 19535 § 3, 2022:  Ord. 18821 § 2, 2018:  Ord. 17934 § 2,
2014:  Ord. 17292 § 29, 2012:  Ord. 15958 § 2, 2007:  14263 § 2, 2001:  Ord.
13325 §§ 1 and 2, 1998.  Formerly K.C.C. 4.94.010).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>4A.670.300 
C&amp;D wastes disposal (construction and demolition wastes disposal) – fee –
use.</b>  The fee imposed on the disposal of C&amp;D wastes generated in the
county's jurisdiction under K.C.C. 10.30.050 is thirteen dollars per ton.  All
fee amounts remitted to the solid waste division shall be deposited in a
subfund within the solid waste operating fund established in K.C.C. 4A.200.700,
to be used for the purposes stated in K.C.C. 10.30.050.  (Ord. 19805 § 2, 2024: 
Ord. 18166 </span><span lang=ES-MX style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 5, 2015).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<h1><a name="_Toc54697865"><span style='font-size:12.0pt'>4A.675           REAL
ESTATE SERVICES FEES</span></a></h1>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoBodyText3><span style='font-size:12.0pt'>            4A.675.010    Easement
application fee.</span></p>

<p class=MsoBodyText3><span style='font-size:12.0pt'>            4A.675.020    Franchise
application – new, amended, renewal, extension,                                                  advertising
fees – surcharge for costs and expenses.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.675.030    Right-of-way
construction permit processing fees.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.675.040    Special
use permit application fee.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.675.050    Wireless
right-of way use agreement application processing and                                            coordinating
fee - surcharge.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4A.675.060    Continuing
use of rights-of-way-annual use payment.</span></p>

<p class=MsoBodyText3><span style='font-size:12.0pt'>            4A.675.070    Utility
construction work and installation, and other uses, upon, along,                                 over,
under or across any public place that is not a right-of-way fee.</span></p>

<p class=MsoBodyText3><span style='font-size:12.0pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>4A.675.010 
Easement application fee.</b>  The easement application fee for a party
requesting a new easement, amended easement or easement transfer under K.C.C.
4.56.115 is three thousand dollars, plus actual costs and all expenses incurred
by the real estate services section in excess of this fee as specified in
K.C.C. 4.56.115.  (Ord. 17691 § 2, 2013:  Ord. 17691 § 2, 2013:  Ord. 17515 §
2, 2013).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>4A.675.020 
Franchise application – new, amended, renewal, extension, advertising fees –
surcharge for costs and expenses.</b></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  The
franchise application fee for a party requesting a new franchise, an amended
franchise, a renewal or extension of an existing franchise or a transfer of its
franchise rights under K.C.C. 6.27.054 is two thousand five hundred dollars.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  The
advertising fee under K.C.C. 6.27.054 is the full advertising costs associated
with the application.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  The real
estate services section of the facilities management division may assess a
surcharge to recover the actual costs as specified in K.C.C. 6.27.054.B.  (Ord.
18403 § 2, 2016:  Ord. 17691 § 3, 2013:  Ord. 17515 § 4, 2013).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>4A.675.030 
Right-of-way construction permit processing fees.</b></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  The
right-of-way construction permit application fee for a party requesting a
permit under K.C.C. chapter 14.44, is two hundred dollars, as specified in
K.C.C. 14.44.040.A.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  The real
estate services section of the facilities management division may assess a
surcharge to recover the actual costs as specified in K.C.C. 14.44.040.B.  (Ord.
18403 § 3, 2016:  Ord. 17691 § 5, 2013:  Ord. 17515 § 8, 2013).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>4A.675.040 
Special use permit application fee.</b>  The fee for a special use permit
application shall be five hundred dollars.  (Ord. 17515 § 6, 2013).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>4A.675.050 
Wireless right-of way use agreement application processing and coordinating fee
- surcharge.</b></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  The
application fee for a party requesting a wireless right-of-way use agreement as
provided in K.C.C. 14.45.080, is five hundred dollars.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  The real
estate services section of the facilities management division may assess a
surcharge to recover costs as specified in K.C.C. 14.45.080.B.  (Ord. 17691 §
6, 2013:  Ord. 17515 § 11, 2013).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>4A.675.060 
Continuing use of rights-of-way-annual use payment.</b></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  The annual
use payment for continuing use of the county rights-of-way for wireless
communications facilities shall be the following amounts for 2017 and, for each
year thereafter, the 2017 amount adjusted as provided in subsection C. of this
section:</span></p>

<table class=MsoNormalTable border=1 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0
